<title>UK: Bradford &amp; Bingley sets 100 mln stg bond.</title>
<headline>Bradford &amp; Bingley sets 100 mln stg bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following subordinated step-up</p>
<p>callable bond was announced by lead manager HSBC.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BRADFORD AND BINGLEY BUILDING SOCIETY</p>
<p> AMT    100 MLN STG   COUPON     **	  MATURITY    07.JUN.07</p>
<p> TYPE   STEP-UP	 ISS PRICE  **	  PAY DATE   L21.MAY.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  40 BP     REOFFER    **	  SPREAD	+70 BP</p>
<p> NOTES	** TO BE PRICED</p>
<p>	    L-LONG FIRST COUPON</p>
<p>	    *CALL AT PAR FROM 07.JUN.02</p>
<p> MOODY	A3	  LISTING    LONDON    PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  =	   DENOMS (K) 100	 SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   IPMA (2)</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  BRITISH   TAX PROVS   STD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    20 BP     SELL CONC  20 BP     PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 7.0 PCT 2002 GILT</p>
<p> NOTES	IF NOT CALLED AT PAR ON 07.JUN.02, COUPON WILL BE</p>
<p>RESET</p>
<p>		AT 120 BP OVER THE PREVAILING FIVE-YEAR GILT</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
